### AutoQuant-AI Backend API requests
### Open with the VS Code "REST Client" extension or httpyac, then send each request.
###
### Start the server first:
###   uv run python main.py
### (requires the env vars in .env; provider keys are checked at startup by app/deps.py)

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000

### 1. Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### 2. Global market holder index summary (symbols indexed, per-exchange counts,
###    primary venue counts)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/market/index

### 2b. Full routing index sample (symbol -> best + all listing exchanges)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/market/index?quote=USDT&limit=20

### 2c. Routing for one symbol across all exchanges that list it
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/market/index?symbol=BTC/USDT

### 3. Exchange routing for a symbol (best-first by liquidity / quote / priority)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/market/routes?symbol=BTC/USDT

### Routing for a symbol that may not be on Binance
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/market/routes?symbol=SOL/USDT

### 4. List active trading symbols in the DB
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/symbols

### 5. Add a trading symbol
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/symbols
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "symbol": "BTC/USDT",
  "asset_class": "crypto",
  "category": "spot"
}

### 6. Deactivate a trading symbol
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/symbols?symbol=BTC/USDT

### 7. Current paper-trading portfolio state
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/portfolio

### 8. Recent orders (from PostgreSQL)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders?limit=20

### 9. Run a backtest
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/backtest
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "symbol": "BTC/USDT",
  "days": 30,
  "strategy": "sentiment_momentum"
}

### 10. Kick off AI research & strategy evolution in the background
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/research/run?symbol=BTC/USDT

### 11. Multi-agent market consensus (technical + sentiment + macro + CRO)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/agents/consensus?symbol=BTC/USDT

### 12. Execute the multi-agent StateGraph workflow trace
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/graphs/workflow?symbol=BTC/USDT

### 13. WebSocket live market + order feed
### (not supported by REST Client; use a WS client, e.g.: wscat -c ws://localhost:8000/ws/live)
WS {{baseUrl}}/ws/live